			<item>
				<title>Software</title>
				<link>http://localhost:1313/software/</link>
				<pubDate>Sat, 17 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid>http://localhost:1313/software/</guid>
				<description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;software-r-packages&#34;&gt;&#xA;  R Packages&#xA;  &lt;a class=&#34;heading-link&#34; href=&#34;#software-r-packages&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;i class=&#34;fa-solid fa-link&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34; title=&#34;Link to heading&#34;&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&#xA;    &lt;span class=&#34;sr-only&#34;&gt;Link to heading&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;tumr&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Tools for visualization and statistical modeling of longitudinal tumor growth data in mouse models.&lt;br&gt;&#xA;&lt;a href=&#34;https://github.com/pbreheny/tumr&#34;  class=&#34;external-link&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;[GitHub]&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a href=&#34;https://github.com/pbreheny/tumr&#34;  class=&#34;external-link&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;[CRAN]&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;qast&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;A Quality Adjustment Survival Tool for a Patient-centered Personalized Care in Oncology.&lt;br&gt;&#xA;&lt;a href=&#34;https://github.com/Gapomochi/qast&#34;  class=&#34;external-link&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;[GitHub]&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;r-shiny&#34;&gt;&#xA;  R Shiny&#xA;  &lt;a class=&#34;heading-link&#34; href=&#34;#r-shiny&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;i class=&#34;fa-solid fa-link&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34; title=&#34;Link to heading&#34;&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&#xA;    &lt;span class=&#34;sr-only&#34;&gt;Link to heading&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;/h2&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>About</title>
				<link>http://localhost:1313/about/</link>
				<pubDate>Wed, 14 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid>http://localhost:1313/about/</guid>
				<description>&lt;p&gt;I am a PhD student in &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.public-health.uiowa.edu/biostat/&#34;  class=&#34;external-link&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;Biostatistics&lt;/a&gt; at the University of Iowa, where I am receiving rigorous training in statistics. I work as a research assistant in the Biostatistics Core at the &lt;a href=&#34;https://holden.uihealthcare.org/research/mogs-and-spores/neuroendocrine-tumors-spore&#34;  class=&#34;external-link&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;Holden Comprehensive Cancer Center&lt;/a&gt;. I have been fortunate to receive guidance from Drs. &lt;a href=&#34;https://emilykroberts.github.io/&#34;  class=&#34;external-link&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;Emily Roberts&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&#34;https://pbreheny.org/web/&#34;  class=&#34;external-link&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;Patrick Breheny&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.public-health.uiowa.edu/faculty/gideon-zamba/&#34;  class=&#34;external-link&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;Gideon Zamba&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.mayo.edu/research/faculty/zahrieh-david-m-ph-d/bio-20528095&#34;  class=&#34;external-link&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;David Zahrieh&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;My undergraduate major was Financial Engineering (within the field of Economics), and I previously worked as a quantitative researcher, focusing on high-frequency trading using methods such as stochastic analysis and reinforcement learning. Over time, I realized that I was more interested in applying statistical methods to address biomedical problems.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>Publications</title>
