				<description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;publication-preprints&#34;&gt;&#xA;  In preparation&#xA;  &lt;a class=&#34;heading-link&#34; href=&#34;#publication-preprints&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;i class=&#34;fa-solid fa-link&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34; title=&#34;Link to heading&#34;&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&#xA;    &lt;span class=&#34;sr-only&#34;&gt;Link to heading&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;T. Zhao&lt;/strong&gt; and P. Breheny (2026). Visualization and Statistical Modeling of Longitudinal Tumor Growth in Mouse Models.&lt;br&gt;&#xA;&lt;a href=&#34;https://github.com/pbreheny/man-tumr&#34;  class=&#34;external-link&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;[paper]&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a href=&#34;https://github.com/pbreheny/tumr&#34;  class=&#34;external-link&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;[software]&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;T. Zhao&lt;/strong&gt;, D. Zahrieh, and G. K. D. Zamba (2026). What Are the Optimal Utilities in Q-TWiST? A New Patient-Centered Quality-Adjusted Survival Metric Framework for Comparative Treatment Benefit.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;publication-published&#34;&gt;&#xA;  Peer-reviewed Publications&#xA;  &lt;a class=&#34;heading-link&#34; href=&#34;#publication-published&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;i class=&#34;fa-solid fa-link&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34; title=&#34;Link to heading&#34;&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&#xA;    &lt;span class=&#34;sr-only&#34;&gt;Link to heading&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;E. M. Voigt, A. L. Isaacson, M. R. Leidinger, J. A. Goeken, Q. Hanigan, D. F. Guo, R. M. Gasser, M. Eadie, I. Babor, B. W. Darbro, W. Paradee, K. Rahmouni, &lt;strong&gt;T. Zhao&lt;/strong&gt;, P. Breheny, E. Lee, M. Kim, D. K. Meyerholz, M. Milhem, R. D. Dodd, and D. E. Quelle (2026). Development of a Cre-inducible Rabl6a transgenic mouse model that enhances sarcoma growth in vivo. &lt;em&gt;Cancers&lt;/em&gt;, 18(14), 2230.&lt;br&gt;&#xA;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.mdpi.com/2072-6694/18/14/2230&#34;  class=&#34;external-link&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;[paper]&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
